- UNCOMMITTED NOT SURFACED: repos with working state the briefing never names: {{REPO_DIR}}
- transcript ground truth omitted from this audit: provider hardening is off or the CLI is not Claude-shaped, so the prompt would be persisted as a new transcript.
- SHA-grounding (deterministic — cited SHAs only; the judge additionally weighs cited FILES): FAIL
- popup available for comparison: not configured (--popup=<dir> to enable)

## Adversarial judge (claude — holistic; its Ground verdict also considers files)
You are an ADVERSARIAL evaluator of a developer's git-based "daily briefing". Attack it from
multiple angles — do NOT be charitable. Find what it got wrong, missed, or could do better, grounded
ONLY in the evidence below. Never invent facts not present here.

